{
 "_comment": "🏷 Tags — the cross-shelf layer (WO-15). A shelf says what KIND of place this is; a facet says whether THAT branch is worth walking to; a tag says what a place ALSO is, across every shelf: vegan, bitcoin, wifi, wheelchair, open 24 h, inside the moat, 7-Eleven, royal temple. Every tag here is DERIVED by exactly one rule from a field the record already carries — nothing is typed onto a place, nothing is inferred from a name or a category except where the rule says so in so many words. The vocabulary was MINED from the catalogue (16,270 records, 140 attrs keys, 2026-08-19): a tag is defined below only where the data already answers for it. tags_layer.py reads this file; `tags` + `tagVia` land on each record in data/places.json; pages are /<prov>/tag/<slug>.html and /tags.html. Curated tags (a person's own list) go in data/curated/tags_curated.json, and curated outranks derived.",
 "_rule_kinds": {
  "attr": "attrs[key] is a string (or ';'-joined string): tag when any token is in `values`. `values` are compared casefolded.",
  "attr-dict": "attrs[key] is a dict (diet, payment): tag when attrs[key][sub] is in `values`.",
  "attr-list": "attrs[key] is a list (crypto, fuel, specialty): tag when any item is in `values`.",
  "attr-true": "attrs[key] is boolean true (inOldCity, highland, borderland).",
  "facet": "the record's facet dict (attrs.facets, OSM-derived) or an owner's tick in claims.json carries this facet key. Provenance rides along: osm-tag / osm-near / field.",
  "moat": "Chiang Mai only — the pin lies inside the old-city moat quadrilateral (build.MOAT_POLY), or the record already says inOldCity. Computed, never typed.",
  "royal": "build.royal_of(r) — the temple is on the hand-kept royal list in data/curated/honours.json (every entry has a fetched source URL).",
  "food-award": "build.FOOD_BY_ID — a food mark in honours.json whose award key starts with `prefix`.",
  "brand": "generated at build from attrs.brand / brandTh / brandEn via build._brand_index (the corpus's own say-so), one tag per chain with at least brand_min branches in the province. Not listed below one by one — 144 chains would go stale the day a new one is crawled.",
  "field": "presence or absence of fields the record itself carries — `need` all present, `lack` all absent, `max_present` at most N of `of`. Describes the RECORD, not the place: a stub is a thin entry here, never a claim about the shop.",
  "hours": "parsed from the record's `hours` string (OSM opening_hours syntax): `weekday` the day must appear, `closes_after` / `opens_before` an HH:MM the span must cross. Unparseable strings earn nothing.",
  "mined": "generated by tags_mine.py from the field's OWN values across the corpus — one tag per value with at least `min` records. Listed under `mined` below, not one by one: 388 Overture categories and 1,782 trade words would go stale the day the next crawl lands."
 },
