 "mined": [
  {
   "key": "cuisine-overture",
   "source": "attrs.overtureCategory",
   "min": 5,
   "family": "cuisine",
   "glyph": "🍜",
   "only_suffix": [
    "_restaurant"
   ],
   "strip_suffix": true,
   "map_existing": true,
   "_note": "The 46 *_restaurant words in the Overture fold are cuisines, not kinds: 5,026 records. Minted as kinds they stood beside the hand-written cuisine list saying the same thing twice — japanese_restaurant beside japanese. strip_suffix names them by the cuisine; map_existing hands the records to the tag that already exists rather than minting its twin. Runs before the kind family so those values are spoken for once."
  },
  {
   "key": "kind",
   "source": "attrs.overtureCategory",
   "min": 5,
   "family": "kind",
   "glyph": "🧭",
   "skip_values": [
    "eat_and_drink",
    "food",
    "shopping",
    "accommodation",
    "education",
    "professional_services",
    "business_to_business",
    "structure_and_geography"
   ],
   "_note": "The Overture fold's own category word. 63,170 records carry it and nothing read it; 18,730 of those stand on a shelf with no sub-shelf, so this is the only fine grain they have. skip_values are the nine that only restate the shelf they are already filed on. 2026-09-08: map_existing so a category that says what a hand-written tag already says joins it (bubble_tea → bubble-tea) instead of standing beside it; floor 8 → 5, which is the same floor the other fields use. 2026-09-08: `restaurant` un-skipped. It was skipped as a restatement of the food shelf, and for a record with a sub-shelf it is one — but 3,873 records carry it and NO sub, so it was the only word they had, and 'restaurant' is a word readers type. The vaguer eight (shopping, accommodation, education, professional_services, business_to_business, structure_and_geography, food, eat_and_drink) stay skipped: they name the shelf and nothing else.",
   "map_existing": true
  },
  {
   "key": "sub",
   "source": "sub",
   "min": 5,
   "family": "kind",
   "glyph": "🧭",
   "map_existing": true,
   "_note": "The sub-shelf the record already stands on, read as a tag. 87,319 records carry one and the tag layer read none of them, so a massage shop with a technique (tok-sen), a hotel with a class (hotel-full) and a food stall with a cuisine (thai) all arrived with nothing to be found by across shelves. map_existing means the sub joins the tag that already says it — sub `cafe` is the cafe tag, sub `thai` is the Thai cuisine tag — so this adds an axis rather than a second vocabulary. It does duplicate the sub-shelf pages, which is Nan's call to keep or drop: 2026-09-08, 'tag every record you can — make tags prolific'."
  },
